female breast cancer is now the number  one cancer diagnosis  worldwide what's new for the first time  female breast cancer has surpassed  lung cancer as the most commonly  diagnosed cancer type in the world  denise valdez tells us now more than  ever  women need to do regular screenings and  breast self-exams  now when that report was published in  the cancer journal for clinicians  it was a real eye-opener breast cancer  is more common in women  than lung cancer now remember some  breast cancer risk factors  family history and age for example can't  be changed  but steps can be taken to lower risk  including weight control  limiting alcohol intake regular exercise  and breast cancer screening  patty crowl is a mammography supervisor  at desert radiology  if she knows her own body she's going to  notice those tiny little changes that  your fingers are going to tell your  brain hey back up i feel something  and that's usually the first time they  notice there's something not quite right  it may be benign but it's not worth  taking a chance  it's especially important for women with  dense breast tissue which affects about  half of women under 50. it can make it  difficult to spot cancers on mammograms  it also increases the risk for  developing cancer because the cells in  the glands tend to divide frequently  leading to mistakes or mutations  mammograms are very simple  they're really not that uncomfortable  it's a very short window of time it's  very small radiation  and it can save your life women who've  been told that they have  dense breasts might want to speak to  their doctor about the best screening  strategy for their needs especially  since  other factors like age or medical  history may also impact their overall  risk  for buddy check denise valdez 8 news now
 

